From db76c240838e0e04fbbb9bdf6f28bcdff64b0c8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:35:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(delegation): a background subagent stopped by gateway
 shutdown wakes its parent [daveey]

A core update restarted the gateway while a background subagent waited on CI. The shutdown sweep
stopped it with the same cooperative stop /stop uses, so its result read 'interrupted' like a
requested stop: the unviewed local parent got a silent note, ran no turn, and the user heard
nothing until he asked (self-heal defect agent-b24ce546ae).

- async_delegation.interrupt_all(reason, by_shutdown=True) stamps each running unit; the
  completion event carries interrupted_by=<reason> (persisted, so the post-restart replay has it).
  /stop, CLI exit and interrupt_for_session (chat closed, /new) stay unstamped.
- gateway/run_shutdown passes by_shutdown=True.
- delegation_wakes_parent counts an interrupted/cancelled child as failed when interrupted_by is
  set (as it already does for the stall monitor's stop); the result text says it was stopped by
  the shutdown, not the user: re-dispatch or tell the user.
- Detection: WARNING 'parent <sid> not woken: ...' when a local result with unfinished children
  will not wake its parent, and when a waking result is kept as a note (chat closed / wake limit).

Tests: tests/tools/test_delegate_shutdown_stop_wakes_parent.py (new), shutdown-sweep case in
tests/gateway/test_shutdown_kill_restart_source.py, replayed shutdown result runs as a turn in
tests/gateway/test_unviewed_delegation_failure_turn.py. 7 fail on the base, all pass after.
